 "doc": "Hadley edge clamped to [10, 90] degrees of a seeded table of 400 random bodies (period of either sign, radius, gravity, scale height log-uniform), which crosses every clamp and the eddy threshold: no spin gives 90, a tiny edge 10. Float64, rtol 1e-9; the clamp makes it exact where it bites. A non-finite raw edge (no spin, an infinite gravity or scale height, a NaN radius) gives 90 (the test is isfinite, not == inf). NaN and infinities may appear in the inputs (a rotation period None is stored as NaN) and in the outputs: NaN equals NaN, an infinity equals the same infinity (sign included).",
